    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Men\nAug: 14,1979\nSFO - IAD\n(via PHX)\nASSORTED HORS D'OEUVRES\nChilled Jumbo Sno Crab Claws\nDeviled Egg Halves Medallions of Chicken Galantine\nAMERICAN GREEN SALAD\nFresh garden greens tossed with shredded carrots and red cabbage,\ngarnished with sliced mushrooms, alfalfa sprouts and ripe tomato wedges, served with a choice of dressings.\nOVEN-WARMED BREADS, SOUR DOUGH ROLLS AND BISCUITS SERVED WITH BUTTER.\nENTREE SELECTION\nSTUFFED DOUBLE PORK CHOP\nSPLIT CRAB LEGS\nFresh, succulent pork chop, delicately seasoned,\nAlaskan crab legs specially prepared\nlightly grilled, then slowly simmered in its own natural juices.\nin a rich butter sauce with just a hint of garlic.\nCHATEAUBRIAND\nFRESH FRUIT SALAD\nThe center cut of the filet, carefully roasted and\nSeasonal fruits and cottage cheese\ncarved to order. Served with a creamy sauce Persain\non a bed of crisp, fresh greens, garnished with chopped\naccented with a touch of brandy.\nEnglish walnuts and served with tangy fruit dressing.\nPOTATO AND VEGETABLE SELECTED ACCORDING TO SEASON.\nFROM OUR DESSERT CART\nICE CREAM FESTIVAL\nFrench vanilla ice cream with your choice of\nstrawberry, butterscotch or hot fudge topping, and chopped walnuts.\nOr enjoy your favorite cordial over ice cream.\nFRESHLY BREWED COFFEE Sanka TEA OR MILK\nAFTER DINNER MINT\nIf by chance your choice is not available due to previous passenger selection, please accept our apology.\nFrom the list below we have selected for your flight today\na white wine, a red wine and Hanns Kornell Champagne.\nThese fine West Coast wines were specially chosen by\nwine author and consultant to American Airlines, Creighton Churchill.\nWHITE WINES\nRED WINES\nJOHANNISBERG RIESLING, ESTATE BOTTLED, 1977\nFrom Sonoma Vineyards, Windsor, California.\nRich and satisfying, ideal with chicken\nand fish dishes-from one of California's\ntraditionally finest wine regions.\nSEMILLON, 1977\nFrom Ste. Michelle Vineyards, Woodinville, Washington.\nAn outstanding product of America's\nfast-developing Northwest wine industry.\nSoft and gentle.\nIOHANNISBERG RIESLING, 1977\nFrom San Martin Vineyards, San Martin, California.\nThe prized Riesling grape of Germany is responsible for this\ncharmingly fragrant and fruity wine,\nmade in Santa Clara County south of San Francisco.\nZINFANDEL, 1975\nFrom Wente Bros., Livermore, California.\nThe Zinfandel grape, unique to California,\nproduces a red wine with a deep color and\nan intriguing \"brambley\" flavor akin to wild blackberries.\nPINOT NOIR, 1975\nFrom Simi Vineyards, Healdsburg, California.\nTransplanted to California, Burgundy's Pinot Noir\nmakes a smooth and pleasing wine,\noftentimes much resembling its noble European counterpart.\nCABERNET SAUVIGNON, 1977\nFrom Fetzer Vineyards, Mendocino County, California.\nIndisputably California's most distinguished red wines,\nCabernet Sauvignons rest in oak casks for months\nbefore gaining their robust, vibrant character.\nCHAMPAGNE\nEXTRA DRY CALIFORNIA CHAMPAGNE\nFrom the Hanns Kornell Champagne Cellars at St. Helena, Napa Valley, California.\nNo other U.S. Champagne has received as many awards,\nboth here and abroad, as Hanns Kornell.\nServed continuously on American Airlines for more than a decade.",
      "AmericanAirlines\n2001.039.163",
      "The\nBeauty\nof Flight,"
    ],
